		{ src: 'https://cdn.sanity.io/images/rusi1hyi/production/1a4c78f5c75a1715af80cb4aa20a65fa96462614-1880x1253.jpg', alt: 'A white clapboard church in New England in autumn' },
	]}
	galleryBottomCreditHtml={`Photos via <a href="https://www.pexels.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--color-brand);" class="hover:underline">Pexels</a> &amp; <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--color-brand);" class="hover:underline">Wikimedia Commons</a>.`}
	faithHeading="Faith and the Bible in the United States"
	faithBodyHtml={`<p>America is, by the numbers, a Christian nation. About <strong>62% of Americans identify as Christian</strong> &mdash; and the US is among the world&rsquo;s largest Bible-publishing nations. Most households have several.</p><p>But the thread is fraying. The fastest-growing group is the religiously unaffiliated &mdash; the &ldquo;nones,&rdquo; now around 29% &mdash; and weekly church attendance keeps falling. Millions own a Bible they rarely open, and know God more as a distant idea than as a near Father.</p><p>That is America&rsquo;s real need. Not another Bible on the shelf &mdash; but to meet, in the one it already owns, the Father who has been there all along.</p>`}
	sources={[
		{ label: 'World Bank, Population, total (2024) — compiled from UN World Population Prospects 2024 and national statistics offices', url: 'https://data.worldbank.org/indicator/SP.POP.TOTL?locations=US' },
		{ label: "Pew Research Center, Religious Landscape Study 2023-24 (February 2025): 62% of U.S. adults Christian, 29% religiously unaffiliated", url: "https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/2025/02/26/religious-landscape-study-executive-summary/" },
		{ label: 'Religion in the United States (Pew)', url: 'https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/religious-landscape-study/' },
		{ label: 'United States — Encyclopaedia Britannica', url: 'https://www.britannica.com/place/United-States' },
	]}
	painsHeading="What pains America"
	painsIntroHtml={`Behind the abundance, America carries deep and hidden wounds &mdash; and it is into these exact wounds that the Father&rsquo;s heart speaks.`}
	painStats={[
		{ value: 'nearly 1 in 4', label: 'children grow up without a father (biological, step, or adoptive) in the home (Census Bureau, 2023)' },
		{ value: '~19 million', label: 'children live in homes without a father — a fatherlessness epidemic' },
		{ value: '~80,000', label: 'lives lost to drug overdose in 2024 (CDC provisional; 110,000 in 2023) — deaths of despair' },
		{ value: 'a loneliness', label: 'epidemic now declared a public-health crisis by the Surgeon General' },
		{ value: 'rising', label: 'anxiety, depression, and suicide — especially among the young' },
		{ value: '~29%', label: 'now claim no religion — a generation drifting from faith' },
	]}
	painsBodyHtml={`<p>America&rsquo;s deepest crisis is not material but relational: a fatherlessness epidemic, an official loneliness crisis, deaths of despair, and a generation drifting from faith. Beneath the world&rsquo;s wealthiest nation runs a profound ache to be known and loved.</p><p>These are not statistics to a Father. They are sons and daughters He longs to gather. America does not need more abundance &mdash; it needs to know it is held by a Father who never leaves.</p>`}
